00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:03.480
Please, you'll hurt someone!

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.900
Start with a bowl of washed and drained strawberries!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.530
Top with condensed milk
and you're done!

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.940
I'm not comfortable calling
this "cooking" anymore.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.160
Oh, sowwy-wowwy-woo!

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:20.200
Becky thought the <i>condensed</i> milk jugs
would give condensed milk!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.000
So confusing!

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.330
I'm telling you...

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.870
My chest is not "condensed".

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.590
It just looks small compared to Chubby and the tits monster.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:29.210
Who you callin' Chubby?!

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:30.630
Who are you calling a tits monster?!

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:34.590
Sensei, you're really on Ringo-chan's case today. What's the matter?

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.090
I'm jealous of that bitch!

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:37.350
Sorry I asked!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.970
You titless twerp!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.270
Don't let your youth go to your head!

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:44.230
Before you came, <i>I</i> was the school idol!

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.520
Where did you get <i>that</i> idea?

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:46.600
Kiss me!

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:47.230
Like hell!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:48.720
Fine then.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:52.190
Today's main course...

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.450
will be <i>you</i>, wench!

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:58.000
You'll make a fine cut of lean breast meat!

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.870
Not if I get you first.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:02.910
Wai—

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.160
Cut it out, you two.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.370
Hold it right there!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.590
Disputes in Home Ec.
should be settled appropriately.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.170
We'll resolve this with a cooking contest!

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.550
First up, Kinoshita Ringo!

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:22.640
Miso soup?

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:25.310
Pretty basic, isn't it?

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.900
Well, I reckon it was a safe choice.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.860
No solid ingredients except tofu.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:34.370
She used red miso to suit our tastes.

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:36.030
Well, she's ticked all the boxes.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.110
Now for the all-important taste.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.580
What <i>is</i> this taste?

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:48.120
A strange seafood taste,
reminiscent of fish stock,

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.540
plus the powerful fermented taste of naturally brewed miso.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.880
The taste lacks cohesiveness for sure,

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:54.960
yet I'm somehow compelled to keep drinking.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.170
What is this dense and complex taste?

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:02.100
This far transcends
the realm of "miso soup"!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:05.680
Surely this liquid is the primeval soup!

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.770
And here I merely
thought it tasted funny.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:13.570
Kinda sour, and fishy to boot.

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:17.650
Ringo-chan, what stock did you use in this miso soup?

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.280
Indoor shoes.

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:25.700
I used a generous amount of the browned part of the insole.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.290
This just gets worse...

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.120
It turned into a really brownish stock.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.490
That's why you used red miso?

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:32.710
To hide it?

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.670
I get the feelin' the contest's already over.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:42.140
It's hard to believe anyone,
even that teacher, can top <i>this</i>.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.560
Let's not be hasty.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.600
Sensei's entry deserves a look.

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:47.770
Sensei, what have you made?

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.640
I have it right here!

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:52.190
Get ready for my ultimate dish!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:56.280
Just rice?

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.820
Um, Sensei, where's the side dish?

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:01.280
The side dish is right here!

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:09.620
That's sick! On so many levels!

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:15.340
Eat up quick, before
the expiry date passes~

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:18.130
Oh you're <i>way</i> past expired!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.260
I don't know how
you're still a teacher!

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:22.590
How have you not
been fired yet?

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:26.220
Becky's daddy is on the
prefectural assembly.

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.060
The mystery has been completely solved.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.850
Come on, class! Eat your teacher up!

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:32.440
No, devour her!

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:33.150
Mainly the boys!

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.090
That's right!

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:42.070
Come here. Your teacher wants to get dirty!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.030
Wha... Hey...

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.200
No—!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:48.540
That's not what I meant by dir—

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.290
Ready, and...

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.250
No!

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:52.040
S-Save me, Paz—

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.460
If you learn to cook tasty meals,

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.210
vegetable sales will increase!

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:02.800
"Home Ec. Let's do this!"

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.940
<i>When all's said and done,
it was a day like any other.</i>

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.060
<i>Absolutely nothing of note happened.</i>

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.820
<i>If I had to make an addendum,</i>

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:21.690
<i>on the way back from
groceries after school...</i>

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.610
Is this the place?

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:26.410
Yeah.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.990
The Minotamo Rock Festival, huh?

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:31.620
Wanna have a look-see at the stage

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:34.170
and maybe participate if we can?

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.710
But none of us have been in a band before.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:39.860
I'm sure the five of us could
make it work somehow.

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:41.060
That's right.

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:43.220
If you don't think we
have the musical chops,

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:45.590
we could always go visual kei and focus on appearance.

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:49.680
The heavy make-up could
also help disguise Kinoshita.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.310
Visual kei, huh?

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.270
That ain't a bad idea!

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:54.980
Visual kei, huh?

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:57.980
Corn, fuck yeah!

00:20:58.440 --> 00:20:59.570
Kinda like that?

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:00.190
Denied.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:03.650
So that's it?

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.190
Pretty small.

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:07.730
But it looks about right for us.

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:08.700
Don't it?

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.200
Let's do it!

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:13.910
Moving on, our next performer is AKB40.

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.250
AKB40?

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:16.960
That's...!

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:22.340
Hi, all!

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.760
I've been waiting for you! Mwah!

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.220
Becky?!

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.390
I see. So <i>that's</i> what it meant.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:30.180
AKB40 stands for...

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:33.180
Aging Kid-sitter Becky, 40 years old!

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:36.890
Please enjoy the next number!

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:39.020
"Ponytail at Forty"!

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:11.070
Thank you!

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:13.160
Thank you, everyone!

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:13.710
W-Wow...

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:15.370
Where'd she learn <i>that</i>?

00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:16.540
Weddings.

00:23:17.870 --> 00:23:20.660
After twenty years of being invited to them as a friend of the bride

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:24.500
and being asked to do something funny at the receptions,

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:29.130
Becky has mastered every stunt and party trick in the book!

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:30.300
I see.

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:34.160
The next number is "Everyday, Aging"!

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:34.800
Please enj—

00:23:37.630 --> 00:23:39.780
"Trunks at School".
